# ripplecheck.list: which checks ("rows") each changed file feeds. Read by ripplecheck.
# One rule a line. Fields split on spaces. " -- " starts a command, run from the repository root.
#
#   row    <ROW> cheap|slow|sweep-only [-- <command>]   every row the project runs, and how its full run starts
#   feed   <glob> <ROW> [-- <targeted command>]          a changed file matching <glob> feeds <ROW>
#   always <ROW> [-- <command>]                          the fixed fast gate: fires on every diff
#   strict <prefix> [<prefix> ...]                       an unmapped changed file under these is red
#
# Globs: * and ? stay inside one folder, ** crosses folders, a trailing / means "everything below".
# Every matching rule fires, not just the first. A slow row with no targeted command is printed OWED.

row  LINT   cheap  -- make lint
row  UNIT   cheap  -- make test
row  E2E    slow   -- make e2e
row  NIGHT  sweep-only

always LINT

feed src/**        UNIT
feed src/api/**    E2E   -- make e2e-api
feed web/**        E2E

strict src/
